{"name":"Riding Boots","hex":"#734a35","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"riding boots","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of riding boot"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/riding_boots"}],"entries":[{"title":"Riding boot","blocks":[{"text":"A riding boot is a boot made to be used for horse riding. The classic boot comes high enough up the leg to prevent the leathers of the saddle from pinching the leg of the rider, has a sturdy toe to protect the rider's foot when on the ground and has a distinct heel to prevent the foot from sliding through the stirrup. The sole is smooth or lightly textured to avoid being caught on the tread of the stirrup in the event of a fall."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Fieldboots.jpg/330px-Fieldboots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riding_boot","wikidata":"Q118532"},{"title":"Boot","blocks":[{"text":"A boot is a type of footwear. Most boots mainly cover the foot and the ankle, while some also cover some part of the lower calf. Some boots extend up the leg, sometimes as far as the knee or even the hip. Most boots have a heel that is clearly distinguishable from the rest of the sole, even if the two are made of one piece. Traditionally made of leather or rubber, modern boots are made from a variety of materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Cliff_Climbers_Combat_boot_Shoes_Blast.png/330px-Cliff_Climbers_Combat_boot_Shoes_Blast.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boot","wikidata":"Q190868"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Paddockboots.jpg/500px-Paddockboots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Paddockboots.jpg/500px-Paddockboots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Paddock style black leather boots, well worn","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APaddockboots.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/HalfChaps1.jpg/500px-HalfChaps1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/HalfChaps1.jpg/500px-HalfChaps1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Half chaps worn over paddock boots duplicate the protection and visual line of a tall boot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHalfChaps1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Blackcowboyboots.jpg/500px-Blackcowboyboots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Blackcowboyboots.jpg/500px-Blackcowboyboots.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Black leather western Cowboy boots with \"walking\" heels.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlackcowboyboots.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/HooksAndBootjack.jpg/500px-HooksAndBootjack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/HooksAndBootjack.jpg/500px-HooksAndBootjack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boot hooks may be required to pull on some riding boots, and a boot jack is often helpful when removing them","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHooksAndBootjack.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Oxhide_boots._Loulan%2C_Xinjiang._Early_Han_220_BCE_-_8_CE.jpg/500px-Oxhide_boots._Loulan%2C_Xinjiang._Early_Han_220_BCE_-_8_CE.jpg?utm_source=en.w